VALUES (
'2026/10/28/the-policy-rate-says-2-25-the-two-year-yield-says-3-37',
'behaviour',
'article',
'The Policy Rate Says 2.25%. The Two-Year Yield Says 3.37%.',
'Ahead of the Bank of Canada decision at 9:45 a.m. ET today, the two-year Government of Canada yield sits 112 basis points above an overnight rate that has not moved since October 2025. Anchoring research suggests which of the two numbers most households carry in their heads.',
'<ul>
<li><strong>The two-year Government of Canada yield is 3.37%, 112 basis points above the 2.25% policy rate,</strong><span> against a gap of 15 basis points on October 31, 2025.</span></li>
<li><strong>Since February 27 the two-year yield is up 98 basis points and the five-year up 91,</strong><span> while the Bank of Canada overnight rate has not changed.</span></li>
<li><strong>Nineteen of 34 economists expect a quarter-point hike to 2.50% today,</strong><span> against 80% who expected a hold in the previous Reuters poll.</span></li>
<li><strong>Anchoring and status quo bias predict that the older, lower number stays in the room,</strong><span> because adjustments away from a salient starting point tend to fall short.</span></li>
<li><strong>The lowest variable mortgage rate is 3.43%,</strong><span> and Ratehub.ca puts it near 3.7% after a quarter-point hike.</span></li>
</ul>',
'<p>The Bank of Canada target overnight rate has stood at 2.25% since the October 2025 cut. The two-year Government of Canada yield closed Monday at 3.37%, 112 basis points higher. On October 31, 2025 the gap was 15 basis points.</p>
<p>The decision arrives today at 9:45 a.m. ET. In a Reuters poll of 34 economists conducted October 21 to 23, 19 expect a quarter-point hike to 2.50%. The previous poll found 80% expecting the rate to hold at 2.25% through the end of 2026.</p>
<p>Bond markets did not wait for the poll to change. From February 27 to October 26 the two-year yield rose 98 basis points, from 2.39% to 3.37%, and the five-year yield rose 91 basis points, from 2.67% to 3.58%. Over the same stretch the policy rate did not move at all.</p>
<div class="hdq-chart">
<div style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d0d0d0;width:100%;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
<div style="background:#f5f5f5;border-bottom:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
<span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#111;letter-spacing:0.02em;">GOC YIELDS VS BOC POLICY RATE</span>
<span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111;">112 BP GAP</span>
<span style="font-size:13px;color:#2e7d32;">▲ 2-YR +98 BP SINCE FEB 27</span>
<span style="font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-left:auto;">DAILY CLOSES &nbsp;|&nbsp; OCT 1, 2025 TO OCT 26, 2026</span>
</div>
